      "description": "Solids burn and ash out in the kiln (often ~ 850–1200 °C). Gases are then held in the secondary chamber; EU rules (Industrial Emissions Directive) require at least 850 °C for 2 s (1100 °C if the waste contains more than 1 % halogenated organics as chlorine) to complete combustion of organic compounds. Rapid quenching afterwards limits dioxin re-formation.",
