  "summary": "A rotary kiln incinerator burns solid, sludge and liquid wastes. Waste fed at the upper end tumbles down the slowly rotating, slightly inclined kiln while it dries, burns and becomes ash. The gases pass to a secondary combustion chamber where an afterburner ensures complete combustion before heat recovery and gas cleaning.",
